// A finger in idle (CONTINUITY.md, A finger on the body): the dome goes its
// way, and a quick stroke that starts on the body is the stroke it is,
// however fast it lets go: the dome carried on by it, then the stroke's own
// reaction. A quick stroke down part way (squashed under it, the base on
// the floor) and just after it let go (carried on down), one up (stretched,
// a ruffle), across each way (leaning that way), one beside the body, on
// the empty screen (nothing: the dome stays, the Mac hears nothing), the
// second of two quick strokes down (from the first's rebound, so it starts
// lower, where the body is: above it, it would be the screen's), then a slow
// stroke down (pressed under it) that ends in the stroke's own reaction
// (affectionate, melted, eyes shut).
